                <pb facs="0277" n="179" xml:id="pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11130: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-27T13:00:00+08:00">August 27, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 27—1:55 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>757. Two Nationalist planes, apparently Douglases, recently delivered, flew over
                    and dropped three bombs which fell in southern part of city this morning at 10
                    o’clock. Planes apparently from Tsinanfu; also used machine gun. Please inform
                    War Department as from Military Attaché. Apparently no great damage was done.
                    One bomb did not explode.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
